{
 "kind": "skeleton",
 "title": "Groups and their items, many groups",
 "caption": "It stands in a rail, the navigation and the content attached, at the body's full width: the rail stands shut to its icons, and on a phone one bar stands at the top. The page level holds the title. Where the groups are many, the part at the left is a data table widget in its LIST layout, under its filter bar: it keeps its search and its paging, and each group is a line, with its name and one fact under it, a line between each two and a band behind the chosen one, as the messages of a mailbox are. It is not the TABLE layout, because the part is narrow and a person picks one group and does not compare them across columns. At a desktop the chosen one stays open at the right while a person goes from one to the next. On a tablet and a phone one part shows at a time: the items of the chosen group take the place of the groups, with a back action before the title, and the groups, with their filter bar, are the screen before it. On a phone the filter bar is one button that says how many filters are on, and the items are the lines of a list, as the groups are.",
